# ESGIQ Platform — Complete Engineering Intelligence Audit
**Generated:** 2026-05-09 | **Auditor:** AI Engineering Analysis | **Codebase Revision:** Post-Final-Polish Phase

---

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

### Actual Current Architecture
ESGIQ is a **pure SPA (Single Page Application)** built with React 18 + Vite 5. There is no backend, no database, and no authentication beyond a UI state flag. The entire application runs inside [AppShell.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/app/AppShell.jsx), which acts as the routing controller using conditional rendering — **no React Router is used for page navigation despite being a dependency**.

### Main Application Flow
```
main.jsx → App.jsx (root) → AppShell.jsx (controls screen/nav state)
                          → LoginPage (screen === 'login')
                          → DashboardLayout (screen === 'app')
                               ├─ Sidebar (nav state)
                               ├─ Topbar (always visible, step state)
                               └─ Content (nav switch)
                                    ├─ DashboardPage
                                    ├─ AssessmentWizardPage (step 1/2/3)
                                    ├─ CertificationsPage
                                    ├─ ReportsPage
                                    └─ SettingsPage
```

### Frontend Stack
| Layer | Technology | Version |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | React | 18.3.1 |
| Build | Vite | 5.4.21 |
| Routing | None (conditional render) | — |
| State | Zustand | 4.5.5 |
| Animation | Framer Motion | ^11 |
| Charts | Recharts | 2.12.7 |
| Icons | Lucide React | 0.441.0 |
| CSS | Custom design system (index.css) | — |
| Type-checking | None (JSX only, no TypeScript) | — |
| Testing | None | — |

### State Management Architecture
Three Zustand stores:
- [ui.store.js](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/store/ui.store.js) — nav, presentationMode, togglePresentation
- [assessment.store.js](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/modules/assessment/store/assessment.store.js) (in modules/) — step, rows, flags with init from MOCK data
- [auth.store.js](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/store/auth.store.js) — exists but **not used anywhere in the app**

### Routing Structure
**No URL-based routing.** [AppShell.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/app/AppShell.jsx) switches between `screen === 'login'` and `screen === 'app'`. Within the app, `nav` state drives which page renders. `react-router-dom` is installed but completely unused. Back/forward browser navigation does nothing.

### Styling System
Single-file CSS design system ([index.css](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/index.css), 802 lines) with:
- CSS custom properties as design tokens
- Utility classes (flex, grid, spacing, typography)
- Component classes (card, badge, btn, sidebar, topbar, progress)
- 8px grid spacing (--sp-1 through --sp-12)

### Animation System
Dual system — a hybrid:
- CSS keyframe `fadeIn` + `.animate-in` class (page transitions)
- Framer Motion: `motion.div`, `AnimatePresence`, `staggerChildren` (dashboard sections, overlay, count-up)
- Inconsistency: some pages use `.animate-in`, dashboard uses Framer Motion

### Charting System
Recharts library, used in:
- [ESGRadarChart.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/components/charts/ESGRadarChart.jsx) (ResultsStep)
- [EmissionsChart.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/components/charts/EmissionsChart.jsx) (unused on main dashboard)
- [TrendAreaChart.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/components/charts/TrendAreaChart.jsx) (unused on main dashboard)
- [ReadinessGauge.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/components/charts/ReadinessGauge.jsx) (unused on main dashboard)

**Critical:** 3 of 4 chart components are defined but not rendered on the main dashboard. Bundle weight incurred without visible value.

### Data Flow Overview
```
Mock Data (INIT_ROWS, INIT_FLAGS) → assessment.store
     → DataUploadStep (user edits rows/flags)
     → useAssessmentScoring(rows, flags) [useMemo hook]
     → scores object → DashboardPage, ResultsStep, SummaryStep
```
All scoring is pure frontend computation. No API call is made at any point during normal usage flow.

### Mock vs Real Logic Identification
| Category | Status |
|---|---|
| Energy scoring | Real calculation, mock default data |
| Water/Waste/Gov scoring | Real calculation, mock default flags |
| Emissions (Scope 1, 2) | Real formula, mock default inputs |
| Scope 3 emissions | **Fake**: hardcoded as 12% of Scope 2 |
| Certification scores | **Fully hardcoded** static arrays |
| Dashboard actions | **Fully hardcoded** static list |
| Benchmark data | **Fully hardcoded** static values |
| Trend data | **Fully hardcoded** static progression |
| Strengths/Gaps in ResultsStep | **Fully hardcoded** static strings |
| Auth | **Fake**: any credentials work |
| Reports download | **Dead**: buttons do nothing |
| Settings toggles | **Dead**: all noop handlers |

