## 8. DESIGN SYSTEM AUDIT

### Spacing Token Consistency
- `--sp-1` through `--sp-12` defined in CSS vars (8px grid). **Note: `--sp-7` and `--sp-8` are both `32px` — redundant duplicate.**
- JS [spacing.js](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/theme/spacing.js) in theme/ defines the same values in JS but is likely never imported (CSS vars used instead). **Dead file.**
- DataUploadStep uses direct style `style={{ maxWidth: 900, margin: '0 auto' }}` — magic number.

### Typography Consistency
- Good CSS class system (`t-micro`, `t-small`, `t-body`, `t-heading` etc.)
- Some inline `fontSize` overrides in components (ESGScoreCard: `fontSize: 48`, StatusBadge inline sizes)

### CSS Variable Integrity
- All core color tokens defined in both CSS vars AND [theme/colors.js](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/theme/colors.js) — **dual-definition system**. Components import `C` from colors.js and use inline styles instead of CSS vars. This is an intentional pattern but creates 2 sources of truth.

### Inline Style Usage (Technical Debt)
Extensive inline styles throughout — not a problem per se given the custom design system, but creates refactor friction:
- DashboardPage: 20+ inline style blocks
- CertificationsPage: 15+ inline style blocks
- ResultsStep: 25+ inline style blocks

### Conflicting CSS Definitions
- `.progress-fill` has `transition: width 0.4s var(--ease)` in CSS AND Framer Motion also controls width. The CSS transition and Framer Motion width animation may conflict on the same element. `overflow: hidden` on `.progress-track` mitigates visual issue.

### Missing Utility Classes
- No `.gap-7` or `.gap-8` (gap-6 is max)
- No responsive breakpoints (`@media` queries) anywhere in CSS
- No dark-mode toggle support (CSS has no light mode)

