## 11. PERFORMANCE & STABILITY AUDIT

### Bundle Size
```
dist/assets/index.js: 694 KB (minified), 206 KB gzipped
```
**This is borderline large for an SPA.** Primary contributors:
1. **Recharts (~350 KB raw)** — 3 of 4 charts are unused on main dashboard
2. **Framer Motion (~150 KB raw)** — justified by animation quality
3. React + React DOM + Zustand: ~45 KB

**Optimization opportunity:** Dynamic import (`React.lazy`) Recharts-heavy components. Could reduce initial JS by ~30-40%.

### Unnecessary Renders
- [useAssessmentScoring](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/modules/assessment/hooks/useAssessmentScoring.js#13-50) uses `useMemo([rows, flags])` — correctly memoized
- DashboardPage re-renders once when `ready` state changes (overlay completes) — acceptable
- [AppShell.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/app/AppShell.jsx) re-renders when any state changes, triggering all child rerenders — mild concern but typical SPA pattern

### Animation Performance Risks
- `framer-motion` `whileHover` on every action row and cert card — fine at current scale (<10 items)
- ESGScoreCard count-up uses `setInterval` (not RAF) — acceptable for 900ms, but could be smoother using `requestAnimationFrame`
- CSS `.progress-fill` transition AND Framer Motion on same element — potential double-animation conflict

### Memory Risks
- No `useEffect` cleanup issues visible
- ESGProcessingOverlay: two `setTimeout` calls with `clearTimeout` cleanup — correct

### Responsive Design
- **App is NOT responsive.** No `@media` queries exist in CSS. Sidebar is 60px fixed. Grid layout (grid-4, grid-2) will break on tablet/mobile.
- [useResponsive.js](file:///c:/Users/Shalvin/Desktop/esg/frontend/src/hooks/useResponsive.js) hook exists but is never used.
- Presentation Mode partially addresses projector use case but doesn't handle small screens.

### Accessibility Gaps
- No `aria-*` attributes on interactive elements
- Sidebar buttons have `title` attributes — minimum acceptable
- No keyboard navigation support beyond basic HTML
- No focus ring styling
- No ARIA roles on score rings or progress bars
- Contrast ratios may be inadequate for WCAG AA compliance (muted color palette)

